CF-374, completed_at 2026-11-06T08:54:38Z), but NO verdict artifact exists. The tier-2 evaluator sat 20+ minutes in a child poll \"sh -c 'sleep 29; tail -2 /tmp/st3.log; grep -n \"EXIT=\" /tmp/st3.log'\" where /tmp/st3.log is a stale selftest log (mtime 04:00, 487 lines, ends \"SELFTEST: PASS\") that no process held open and that contains ZERO \"EXIT=\" lines — the detector could never fire (parent /proc/io byte-identical across 6 s, zero sockets). Foreman killed the run (rc=143). Guard recorded SKIP for that reason, not for a red gate. Instance recorded as an audit event and cross-referenced to CF-375, which owns the instrument defect.\n\nNot touched: docs/ (the 50 pre-existing module errors are other rows' debt), .coding-hermes/, .gitreins/ beyond tasks.yaml, and the recorded .gitreins/rescued-20261105/ residue (2354 paths, dispositions in events 468/470/477).\n\nSTATUS NOTE (foreman 2026-11-06): the row is deliberately still pending. boardctl refuses --status complete without an --evidence-run-id that resolves to a stored verdict (TR-251), and this tick produced none: the tier-2 evaluator wedged on an unfireable wait (CF-375, 4th instance) and was terminated. The implementation is landed and must NOT be re-implemented or re-dispatched: harvest ONE verdict run at 336e7cd (gitreins task start CF-374 then judge --async CF-374, or a sync judge once the evaluator's wait is fixed) and close the row on it."}
